  "output": {
    "section_id": "ch04.s06",
    "paragraphs": [
      {
        "id": "ch04.s06.p01",
        "sentences": [
          {
            "id": "ch04.s06.p01.01",
            "text": "How does a GPT model turn integer token IDs into the logits that will later drive prediction, and why does that simple-looking code already involve more than 100 million parameters?",
            "type": "C",
            "cites": []
          },
          {
            "id": "ch04.s06.p01.02",
            "text": "The model workflow starts with input IDs, converts them into token embeddings, adds positional embeddings, applies dropout, passes the result through the Transformer block, applies another layer normalization layer, applies an output head layer, and returns the logits.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "G3-JgHckzjw@324",
              "G3-JgHckzjw@327",
              "G3-JgHckzjw@329",
              "G3-JgHckzjw@331",
              "G3-JgHckzjw@333",
              "G3-JgHckzjw@334",
              "G3-JgHckzjw@337",
              "G3-JgHckzjw@339",
              "G3-JgHckzjw@340",
              "G3-JgHckzjw@342",
              "G3-JgHckzjw@345"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "ch04.s06.p01.03",
            "text": "After the input embeddings are formed by combining token embeddings and positional embeddings, the remaining stages are dropout, the Transformer blocks, another layer of normalization, and the output head.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "G3-JgHckzjw@2931",
              "G3-JgHckzjw@2933",
              "G3-JgHckzjw@2948",
              "G3-JgHckzjw@2955",
              "G3-JgHckzjw@2958",
              "G3-JgHckzjw@2962",
              "G3-JgHckzjw@2964",
              "G3-JgHckzjw@2966",
              "G3-JgHckzjw@2972",
              "G3-JgHckzjw@2973",
              "G3-JgHckzjw@2977",
              "G3-JgHckzjw@2979",
              "G3-JgHckzjw@2981",
              "G3-JgHckzjw@2984",
              "G3-JgHckzjw@2986",
              "G3-JgHckzjw@2988"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "ch04.s06.p01.04",
            "text": "An earlier version of the GPTModel class already had a forward method, but its Transformer block and layer normalization were only dummy implementations.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "G3-JgHckzjw@2543",
              "G3-JgHckzjw@2546",
              "G3-JgHckzjw@2549",
              "G3-JgHckzjw@2552",
              "G3-JgHckzjw@2554",
              "G3-JgHckzjw@2556",
              "G3-JgHckzjw@2559"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "ch04.s06.p01.05",
            "text": "Those placeholders were later replaced after coding the layer normalization class, the feed-forward neural network class, and the Transformer class.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "G3-JgHckzjw@2562",
              "G3-JgHckzjw@2564",
              "G3-JgHckzjw@2565",
              "G3-JgHckzjw@2567",
              "G3-JgHckzjw@2570",
              "G3-JgHckzjw@362",
              "G3-JgHckzjw@364",
              "G3-JgHckzjw@368",
              "G3-JgHckzjw@370",
              "G3-JgHckzjw@372"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "ch04.s06.p01.06",
            "text": "The Transformer block class itself was coded in the last step of that sequence.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "G3-JgHckzjw@2696",
              "G3-JgHckzjw@2698",
              "G3-JgHckzjw@2700"
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "ch04.s06.p02",
        "sentences": [
          {
            "id": "ch04.s06.p02.01",
            "text": "The stacked Transformer portion is implemented by chaining multiple TransformerBlock modules with \"nn.Sequential\".",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "G3-JgHckzjw@2990",
              "G3-JgHckzjw@2994",
              "G3-JgHckzjw@2996",
              "G3-JgHckzjw@3009",
              "G3-JgHckzjw@3011",
              "G3-JgHckzjw@3014",
              "G3-JgHckzjw@3016",
              "G3-JgHckzjw@3018"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "ch04.s06.p02.02",
            "text": "In the configuration shown here, the number of layers is 12, so the model chains together 12 Transformer blocks.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "G3-JgHckzjw@2998",
              "G3-JgHckzjw@3000",
              "G3-JgHckzjw@3002",
              "G3-JgHckzjw@3004",
              "G3-JgHckzjw@3005",
              "G3-JgHckzjw@3009",
              "G3-JgHckzjw@3021",
              "G3-JgHckzjw@3023"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "ch04.s06.p02.03",
            "text": "A simple test batch passed through the model produces an output whose last dimension is the vocabulary size, 50257.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "G3-JgHckzjw@3103",
              "G3-JgHckzjw@3106",
              "G3-JgHckzjw@3107",
              "G3-JgHckzjw@3136",
              "G3-JgHckzjw@3137",
              "G3-JgHckzjw@3139",
              "G3-JgHckzjw@3141",
              "G3-JgHckzjw@3143",
              "G3-JgHckzjw@3157",
              "G3-JgHckzjw@3159",
              "G3-JgHckzjw@3162",
              "G3-JgHckzjw@3163"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "ch04.s06.p02.04",
            "text": "The full output tensor has shape 2 by 4 by 50257, corresponding to two batches, four tokens in each batch, and the vocabulary size.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "G3-JgHckzjw@3163",
              "G3-JgHckzjw@3166",
              "G3-JgHckzjw@3170",
              "G3-JgHckzjw@3173",
              "G3-JgHckzjw@3175",
              "G3-JgHckzjw@3177"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "ch04.s06.p02.05",
            "text": "Even this compact implementation has more than 100 million parameters because it includes 12 Transformer blocks, eight steps in each block, expansion and contraction layers inside each block, and additional token and positional embedding parameters.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "G3-JgHckzjw@3197",
              "G3-JgHckzjw@3199",
              "G3-JgHckzjw@3201",
              "G3-JgHckzjw@3203",
              "G3-JgHckzjw@3208",
              "G3-JgHckzjw@3210",
              "G3-JgHckzjw@3211",
              "G3-JgHckzjw@3216",
              "G3-JgHckzjw@3218",
              "G3-JgHckzjw@3221",
              "G3-JgHckzjw@3223",
              "G3-JgHckzjw@3225"
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "ch04.s06.p03",
        "sentences": [
          {
            "id": "ch04.s06.p03.01",
            "text": "To count parameters in code, sum \"p.numel()\" over the model's parameter tensors.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "G3-JgHckzjw@3229",
              "G3-JgHckzjw@3231",
              "G3-JgHckzjw@3233",
              "G3-JgHckzjw@3236",
              "G3-JgHckzjw@3238",
              "G3-JgHckzjw@3241",
              "G3-JgHckzjw@3244",
              "G3-JgHckzjw@3246",
              "G3-JgHckzjw@3248",
              "G3-JgHckzjw@3249"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "ch04.s06.p03.02",
            "text": "That calculation gives 163 million parameters for the implemented model before weight tying.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "G3-JgHckzjw@3252",
              "G3-JgHckzjw@3253",
              "G3-JgHckzjw@3256"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "ch04.s06.p03.03",
            "text": "The model’s parameters come from token embeddings, positional embeddings, Transformer block parameters, and the final layer before the logits.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "Zxf-34voZss@1032",
              "Zxf-34voZss@1035",
              "Zxf-34voZss@1036",
              "Zxf-34voZss@1038",
              "Zxf-34voZss@1040",
              "Zxf-34voZss@1042",
              "Zxf-34voZss@1044"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "ch04.s06.p03.04",
            "text": "The token embedding parameter count is vocabulary size multiplied by embedding dimension, and the positional embedding parameter count is context size multiplied by embedding dimension.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "Zxf-34voZss@1046",
              "Zxf-34voZss@1048",
              "Zxf-34voZss@1051",
              "Zxf-34voZss@1053",
              "Zxf-34voZss@1056",
              "Zxf-34voZss@1058"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "ch04.s06.p03.05",
            "text": "Together, the token and positional embeddings contribute 38.4 million parameters, and those embedding parameters are also optimized during training.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "Zxf-34voZss@1061",
              "Zxf-34voZss@1063",
              "Zxf-34voZss@1066",
              "Zxf-34voZss@1068"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "ch04.s06.p03.06",
            "text": "Inside multi-head attention, the query, key, and value weights are three trainable matrices of size 768 by 768, for 1.77 million parameters.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "Zxf-34voZss@1072",
              "Zxf-34voZss@1074",
              "Zxf-34voZss@1076",
              "Zxf-34voZss@1078",
              "Zxf-34voZss@1081",
              "Zxf-34voZss@1083",
              "Zxf-34voZss@1085",
              "Zxf-34voZss@1087",
              "Zxf-34voZss@1089"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "ch04.s06.p03.07",
            "text": "The multi-head attention block also includes an output head, and the total number of parameters in that block is 2.36 million.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "Zxf-34voZss@1092",
              "Zxf-34voZss@1094",
              "Zxf-34voZss@1100",
              "Zxf-34voZss@1101",
              "Zxf-34voZss@1104",
              "Zxf-34voZss@1109"
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "ch04.s06.p04",
        "sentences": [
          {
            "id": "ch04.s06.p04.01",
            "text": "The feed-forward network uses an expansion-contraction pattern, projecting from the embedding dimension to a hidden layer of four times that size and then compressing back, and it contributes 4.72 million parameters.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "Zxf-34voZss@1110",
              "Zxf-34voZss@1112",
              "Zxf-34voZss@1115",
              "Zxf-34voZss@1117",
              "Zxf-34voZss@1119",
              "Zxf-34voZss@1121",
              "Zxf-34voZss@1123",
              "Zxf-34voZss@1125",
              "Zxf-34voZss@1128",
              "Zxf-34voZss@1130",
              "Zxf-34voZss@1134",
              "Zxf-34voZss@1137",
              "Zxf-34voZss@1139",
              "Zxf-34voZss@1141",
              "Zxf-34voZss@1144",
              "Zxf-34voZss@1145",
              "Zxf-34voZss@1147"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "ch04.s06.p04.02",
            "text": "One Transformer block therefore contributes 2.36 million plus 4.72 million parameters, and across 12 Transformer blocks that totals 85.2 million parameters.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "Zxf-34voZss@1150",
              "Zxf-34voZss@1152",
              "Zxf-34voZss@1153",
              "Zxf-34voZss@1155",
              "Zxf-34voZss@1160",
              "Zxf-34voZss@1161",
              "Zxf-34voZss@1164",
              "Zxf-34voZss@1166",
              "Zxf-34voZss@1167"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "ch04.s06.p04.03",
            "text": "The final layer has embedding dimension multiplied by vocabulary size parameters, which is 38.4 million.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "Zxf-34voZss@1171",
              "Zxf-34voZss@1173",
              "Zxf-34voZss@1174",
              "Zxf-34voZss@1178",
              "Zxf-34voZss@1179",
              "Zxf-34voZss@1181",
              "Zxf-34voZss@1183"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "ch04.s06.p04.04",
            "text": "Adding 38.4 million embedding parameters, 85.2 million Transformer parameters, and 38.4 million final-layer parameters gives about 162 million parameters in total.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "Zxf-34voZss@1183",
              "Zxf-34voZss@1185",
              "Zxf-34voZss@1187",
              "Zxf-34voZss@1190",
              "Zxf-34voZss@1193",
              "Zxf-34voZss@1195",
              "Zxf-34voZss@1197"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "ch04.s06.p04.05",
            "text": "This is why the model being trained is on the order of more than 100 million parameters.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "Zxf-34voZss@1225",
              "Zxf-34voZss@1227",
              "Zxf-34voZss@1229",
              "Zxf-34voZss@1231",
              "Zxf-34voZss@2027",
              "Zxf-34voZss@2029",
              "Zxf-34voZss@2031"
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "ch04.s06.p05",
        "sentences": [
          {
            "id": "ch04.s06.p05.01",
            "text": "The gap between 163 million parameters in this implementation and 124 million parameters in the smallest GPT-2 comes from weight tying.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "G3-JgHckzjw@3264",
              "G3-JgHckzjw@3267",
              "G3-JgHckzjw@3269",
              "G3-JgHckzjw@3271",
              "G3-JgHckzjw@3274",
              "G3-JgHckzjw@3277",
              "Zxf-34voZss@1199",
              "Zxf-34voZss@1201",
              "Zxf-34voZss@1203"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "ch04.s06.p05.02",
            "text": "In the original GPT-2 architecture, weight tying means reusing the token embedding layer weights in the output layer.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "G3-JgHckzjw@3277",
              "G3-JgHckzjw@3279",
              "G3-JgHckzjw@3281",
              "G3-JgHckzjw@3283",
              "G3-JgHckzjw@3285",
              "G3-JgHckzjw@3287",
              "G3-JgHckzjw@3301",
              "G3-JgHckzjw@3304",
              "G3-JgHckzjw@3306",
              "G3-JgHckzjw@3308",
              "G3-JgHckzjw@3310",
              "Zxf-34voZss@1205",
              "Zxf-34voZss@1207",
              "Zxf-34voZss@1211",
              "Zxf-34voZss@1213"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "ch04.s06.p05.03",
            "text": "The token embedding layer and the output layer have the same shape, 50257 by 768, which is why those parameters can be reused.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "G3-JgHckzjw@3331",
              "G3-JgHckzjw@3333",
              "G3-JgHckzjw@3336",
              "G3-JgHckzjw@3338",
              "G3-JgHckzjw@3342",
              "G3-JgHckzjw@3344",
              "G3-JgHckzjw@3346",
              "G3-JgHckzjw@3348"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "ch04.s06.p05.04",
            "text": "If the output-layer parameters are excluded because of weight tying, the total becomes 124 million parameters, matching the GPT-2 model size.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "G3-JgHckzjw@3354",
              "G3-JgHckzjw@3358",
              "G3-JgHckzjw@3359",
              "G3-JgHckzjw@3361",
              "G3-JgHckzjw@3364",
              "G3-JgHckzjw@3366",
              "G3-JgHckzjw@3368",
              "G3-JgHckzjw@3370",
              "G3-JgHckzjw@3372",
              "Zxf-34voZss@1214",
              "Zxf-34voZss@1218",
              "Zxf-34voZss@1221",
              "Zxf-34voZss@1223"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "ch04.s06.p05.05",
            "text": "Weight tying reduces the overall memory footprint and the computational complexity of the model.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "G3-JgHckzjw@3372",
              "G3-JgHckzjw@3376",
              "G3-JgHckzjw@3379",
              "G3-JgHckzjw@3381",
              "G3-JgHckzjw@3400",
              "G3-JgHckzjw@3402",
              "G3-JgHckzjw@3405"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "ch04.s06.p05.06",
            "text": "This implementation keeps separate token embedding and output layers because separate layers give better training and model performance, and the same choice is described as true for modern LLMs as well.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "G3-JgHckzjw@3383",
              "G3-JgHckzjw@3386",
              "G3-JgHckzjw@3388",
              "G3-JgHckzjw@3390",
              "G3-JgHckzjw@3392",
              "G3-JgHckzjw@3394",
              "G3-JgHckzjw@3397",
              "G3-JgHckzjw@3405",
              "G3-JgHckzjw@3408",
              "G3-JgHckzjw@3410"
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "ch04.s06.p06",
        "sentences": [
          {
            "id": "ch04.s06.p06.01",
            "text": "Parameter count also translates directly into storage requirements.",
            "type": "C",
            "cites": []
          },
          {
            "id": "ch04.s06.p06.02",
            "text": "For this model, 163 million parameters require around 600 megabytes of space.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "G3-JgHckzjw@3412",
              "G3-JgHckzjw@3414",
              "G3-JgHckzjw@3418",
              "G3-JgHckzjw@3420",
              "G3-JgHckzjw@3422",
              "G3-JgHckzjw@3424",
              "G3-JgHckzjw@3426"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "ch04.s06.p06.03",
            "text": "Assuming each parameter is a 32-bit float taking 4 bytes, the size is computed by multiplying the total number of parameters by 4, which gives about 620 MB.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "G3-JgHckzjw@3429",
              "G3-JgHckzjw@3431",
              "G3-JgHckzjw@3433",
              "G3-JgHckzjw@3437",
              "G3-JgHckzjw@3439",
              "G3-JgHckzjw@3441",
              "G3-JgHckzjw@3443",
              "G3-JgHckzjw@3445",
              "G3-JgHckzjw@3446",
              "G3-JgHckzjw@3449"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "ch04.s06.p06.04",
            "text": "Even relatively small LLMs therefore require substantial storage, while extremely large models are described as impossible to run on local devices, which is why GPU access is needed.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "G3-JgHckzjw@3452",
              "G3-JgHckzjw@3454",
              "G3-JgHckzjw@3456",
              "G3-JgHckzjw@3459",
              "G3-JgHckzjw@3462",
              "G3-JgHckzjw@3464",
              "G3-JgHckzjw@3467",
              "G3-JgHckzjw@3469",
              "G3-JgHckzjw@3472",
              "G3-JgHckzjw@3473"
            ]
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
